From 2514b0a32fe66eadbd83b8c530259ebed738dcbe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sudharsan Eswaran <eswaran@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 21:28:27 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Bandwidth 320Mhz support for 6GHz
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

1. added missing NL80211_CHAN_WIDTH_320 case
2. added explicit "if nl80211 reports 320 → BANDWIDTH_320" path,
   bypassing the VHT-only vht_oper_chwidth mapping (which has no 320 slot)
3. generic BANDWIDTH_320 now resolves to BANDWIDTH_320_1/_2 before
   the channels_table_6g lookup
4. 320Mhz BW handling is done in operating channel report message construction logic
5. 320Mhz BW handling is done while processing channel selection request message and
   setting the channel
6. 320Mhz BW setting via hostapd CHAN_SWITCH command is handled

Signed-off-by: Sudharsan Eswaran <eswaran@qti.qualcomm.com>
